cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "RegularityStructures: a Lean 4 formalization of the dynamical Φ⁴₃ model via regularity structures"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the renormalised dynamical Φ⁴₃
  model on the three-dimensional torus: convergence, local well-posedness, and global
  dynamics with an invariant measure and stationary solutions. The local theory follows
  Hairer's Theorem 1.15 (A theory of regularity structures, 2014): for smooth
  initial data and explicit renormalisation constants, the solutions of the equation
  driven by mollified space-time white noise converge in probability in a negative
  Hölder–Besov space up to the maximal existence time of the limit, and the limit does
  not depend on the mollifier. A standalone library proves the general theory used:
  the reconstruction theorem, weighted reconstruction, the multilevel Schauder estimate,
  maximal solutions, and Malliavin calculus for white noise. On top of it, the global
  theory after Mourrat–Weber and Moinat–Weber: for every exponent in (-2/3, -1/2) a
  global flow on the Hölder–Besov space, consistent with the local theory, that comes
  down from infinity, is a Feller Markov process and has an invariant measure obtained
  by the Krylov–Bogoliubov procedure, the law of a stationary solution; the uniform
  moment bound for the regularised equations; and the compatibility of the flows across
  Hölder exponents.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
